# xv6-plus build artifacts (regenerated by `make` / scripts/run-tests.sh).
#
# NOTE: this is deliberately NOT a verbatim copy of upstream xv6-riscv's
# .gitignore. Upstream uses a bare `mkfs` pattern, which is safe there
# only because mkfs/mkfs.c was already tracked before that rule was
# added. In this monorepo, where the whole project is added fresh, a
# bare `mkfs` pattern would match the mkfs/ *directory* itself (gitignore
# patterns with no slash match at any depth) and silently exclude
# mkfs/mkfs.c from being committed at all. So that one path is written
# out explicitly instead. For the same reason, the built-user-binaries
# pattern is `user/_*`, not a bare `_*`: a bare `_*` also matches at any
# depth, which would silently exclude hand-written source files whose
# names start with `_` by convention -- e.g. tests/syscall/_helpers.py,
# tests/accounting/_acct_helpers.py (Phase 1/2 test-harness modules,
# `_`-prefixed only to mark "private to this test package", the normal
# Python convention, not build output). Scoping the pattern to `user/`
# -- the only directory where `make` actually produces `_`-prefixed
# *artifacts* (`user/_cat`, `user/_xtrace`, ... per the Makefile's
# `_%: %.o $(ULIB) ...` UPROGS rule) -- ignores exactly the build
# artifacts and nothing else. See docs/upstream-delta.md.

*.o
*.d
*.asm
*.sym
*.img
user/_*
kernel/kernel
mkfs/mkfs
user/usys.S
.gdbinit
TAGS
*~

# Python test-harness caches (scripts/, tests/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
